  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELOC - AN ACOUSTIC DETECTION SYSTEM FOR ELEPHANTS IN INDONESIA AND SRI LANKA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO DEVELOP AND TEST A NEW TECHNOLOGY AND METHODOLOGICAL APPROACH THAT USES ELEPHANT VOCALIZATIONS TO AUTOMATICALLY DETECT AND LOCATE ELEPHANTS IN ORDER TO REDUCE HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC), SUPPORT ANTI-POACHING EFFORTS, AND PROMOTE HUMAN-ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE. PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE: (1) TO EVALUATE ELEPHANT VOCALIZATIONS (2) DEVELOP ELOC HARDWARE AND SOFTWARE (3) TO TEST AND EVALUATE ELOC FUNCTIONALITY IN THE FIELD AND IN FUTURE PHASES OF THIS PROJECT, FULL-SCALE DEPLOYMENT, APPLICATION, AND PROMOTION OF THE ELOC DEVICE. PROJECT ACTIVITIES ARE TO: (1) BUILD AN ELOC DEVICE BASED ON THE PROTOTYPE AND TEST THE SENSITIVITY OF THE DEVICE (2) REDESIGN THE ELOC DEVICE TO WITHSTAND FIELD CONDITIONS INCLUDING HOUSING, COMMUNICATION CAPABILITIES, AND ENERGY SUPPLY (3) DEVELOP SOFTWARE SYSTEMS FOR AUTONOMOUS DETECTION OF ELEPHANT VOCALIZATIONS AND (4) FIELD TEST ELOC DETECTORS IN SUMATRA, INDONESIA.</narrative>
  </description>
